            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case is presented with severe ischemic heart disease and lupus anticoagulant in a 24 year old otherwise healthy male. Anticoagulation was initiated and coronary by-pass grafting was performed. Coronary biopsy showed no signs of arteritis.</AbstractText>
